Package: tate-note
Version: __VERSION__
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-pango-1.0, fonts-noto-cjk
Maintainer: d.suganuma <ds20100531@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: __SIZE__
Description: Vertical writing (tategaki) text editor
 A desktop text editor for Ubuntu that writes top-to-bottom and
 right-to-left in traditional Japanese vertical style. Text is laid
 out with Pango and drawn by the application itself, so the caret,
 line numbers and whitespace marks are placed exactly. Documents open
 in tabs, each with a memo saved alongside it, and a folder pane can
 browse a whole manuscript.
